From 8311326b49809b3a166d582f0c4f519d43f4cf51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Tue, 7 Apr 2026 22:29:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rework securize to property-based toggle with GSI fingerprint
 tracking

Replace the file-based /system/phh/secure gate with an inverted
property-based /metadata/securize_disable gate. Add GSI fingerprint
change detection so PackageManagerService sees mIsUpgrade=true on
real GSI upgrades by setting persist.pm.mock-upgrade, which PMS ORs
into isDeviceUpgrading().

Re-assert the production debuggability spoofing (ro.debuggable=0,
ro.secure=1) inside the securize block now that the shared personal
tier strips them from upstream. Without this, release builds would
ship with ro.debuggable=1 and root detection would trivially flag
the device.

Drop the remaining ro.*.build.type and ro.adb.secure=1 spoofing
lines, the Hide system/xbin/su mount trick, and the phh-securize.sh
product copy. Add model/manufacturer updates to the usb gadget
strings so lsusb reports the spoofed identity.
